o be at least 12 characters with at least 3 character classes, via a libpwquality drop-in (/etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/90-antrieb-policy.conf with minlen=12, minclass=3) enforced through the existing pam_pwquality entries in system-auth/password-auth. Verified enforcement end-to-end via real passwd/PAM flow (short and low-diversity passwords rejected, compliant password accepted). Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id/uptime/config/service baseline, issued a background `reboot`, polled until exec access returned, confirmed boot_id and boot timestamp changed, and re-verified the policy file persisted and PAM enforcement still worked correctly post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected existing pwquality/PAM configuration on node1\",\"Created /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/90-antrieb-policy.conf with minlen=12 and minclass=3\",\"Verified via pwscore that short and low-class-count passwords are rejected and compliant passwords accepted\",\"Created test user pwpolicytest and confirmed real PAM-driven `passwd` flow rejects weak/2-class passwords and accepts a 12+ char 3-class password\",\"Cleaned up test user\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, policy file contents, sshd active status\",\"Triggered a background `reboot` on node1 so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id and uptime -s changed, proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified policy file persisted and sshd active post-restart\",\"Re-ran end-to-end PAM password test (pwpolicytest2) post-restart to confirm policy still enforced\",\"Cleaned up second test user\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Password policy: minimum 12 characters, at least 3 character classes, configured on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-30bc22fb8a534204\",\"cmd-344651ae52214c4d\",\"cmd-2cd221be99ed4094\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed pam_pwquality already wired into system-auth/password-auth, then created pwquality.conf.d/90